.TH "ODIR-DOT-BVFS_LSDIRS" "7" "" "odir 25.1.2+onesimus.0.2.0" "Onesimus Director Commands"
.SH NAME
odir\-dot\-bvfs_lsdirs \- \&.bvfs_lsdirs: List directories using BVFS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\&.bvfs_lsdirs [jobid=<jobid>[,...]] [path=<path>] [pathid=<pathid>] [limit=<limit>] [offset=<offset>] [pattern=<pattern>] [filename=<filename>]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Lists the subdirectories of a directory in the state of a job chain, as a restore file browser needs them. The BVFS cache must have been filled with .bvfs_update first. The directory is given by path= (with a trailing slash, / for the root) or by pathid= from an earlier output; limit= (default 2000) and offset= page through the result.
.PP
Each line has five tab separated columns: PathId, FileId, JobId, LStat and name. The first two lines are . and ..; directories without their own catalog record have FileId and JobId 0. A JobId the console may not see is refused.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.SS "\&.bvfs_lsdirs"
.TP
.B "jobid=<jobid>[,...]"
Job IDs (text; several values separated by commas)
.TP
.B "path=<path>"
Directory (text)
.TP
.B "pathid=<pathid>"
Path ID (number)
.TP
.B "limit=<limit>"
Most rows (number)
.TP
.B "offset=<offset>"
Rows to skip (number)
.TP
.B "pattern=<pattern>"
Name filter (regular expression) (text)
.TP
.B "filename=<filename>"
File name (text)
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B "\&.bvfs_lsdirs jobid=600,615,616 path=/"
the top level directories of a job chain
.TP
.B "\&.bvfs_lsdirs jobid=600,615,616 pathid=7 limit=100"
the first 100 subdirectories of a known path
.SH ORIGIN
Bareos console command.
